ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477245} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fc6a235-aad1-5564-825b-64bf12cd21c1" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eba7fa4b-455f-59ae-9003-2d93eed75911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668026} {:answer/id #uuid "03a41de9-060e-5c57-a3e7-105df7e9a46d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eba7fa4b-455f-59ae-9003-2d93eed75911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668026} :answer-field/id #uuid "8261df59-b744-51bc-bc8b-0cd85502dc8b" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "202bc30a-b4f4-567b-8021-1d6c51e8b85e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34273" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 7{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” is false, while statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions” and “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87ecc4be-4578-57d6-a249-a80e721e206a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447718} {:answer/id #uuid "ef287bfc-2ff4-5b14-b2d5-1bc2198e03c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87ecc4be-4578-57d6-a249-a80e721e206a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447718} :answer-field/id #uuid "128bee5d-a4a7-57a1-ae6a-7583c0f715e8" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbe9b5d3-6adb-5955-bcd2-adef03763ddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447720} {:answer/id #uuid "41f14142-f395-5b2d-97b2-a7334b9547d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41f14142-f395-5b2d-97b2-a7334b9547d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447721} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2ed73d9-5758-5bb8-b978-25fc615c46b3" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448900} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "530e368b-e235-51ad-89b6-cae0058759c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447722} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b0c5a9-4103-56d9-a943-e66ba874a356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "530e368b-e235-51ad-89b6-cae0058759c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447722} :answer-field/id #uuid "114dd27c-9db0-5c20-a81a-10eeefb53fbc" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448901}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c05cb83d-c779-50b1-a772-7d4551eea239" :question/math-academy-id "q-105308" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-16{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 8 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” and “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” are false, while statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b0bd8cc-6ac8-5e72-b06f-73c1654ffe1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461413} {:answer/id #uuid "e80cc002-b38f-5d3e-892e-0841eebc40e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e80cc002-b38f-5d3e-892e-0841eebc40e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461414} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f887e6-6723-5611-bf95-bd986f87144d" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462460} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a81cd52a-c09b-55c3-9802-d94055e5c375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461415} {:answer/id #uuid "4189cfd7-3469-5cbf-a825-c816cd091f10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/r