y/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af32236d-520e-5b71-b7ec-9663a181498c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105310" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+15{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 15 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” is false, while statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions” and “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd10af90-8268-5232-9473-253f1c4a0da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447724} {:answer/id #uuid "f54d7916-c701-5bcb-a279-b7f11eb4abc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd10af90-8268-5232-9473-253f1c4a0da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447724} :answer-field/id #uuid "8de5c39b-5840-5b9e-83f7-46906d6f45f3" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ffcee29-8511-5be3-b402-b9d385d893a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447726} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f44350-5bbe-53da-b5c6-334f8d6ab627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f44350-5bbe-53da-b5c6-334f8d6ab627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447727} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4b40ad-6afb-5fae-9b64-aacae9759675" :answer-field