d, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 9{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-12{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -5 & -12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{1}+2(\\mathbf{0})+5(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$, we get that the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” and “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” are true, while statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241038 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "119902b6-653e-5dd6-8fa5-3d6771e4a1c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447730} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c8f107-a908-59a2-bf5c-916b59b08aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1c8f107-a908-59a2-bf5c-916b59b08aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447731} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9bbe3de-380f-5883-ac7f-def1d9e1b0c6" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5728916d-87d9-52c5-a916-0ccca10350a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447732} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d20f68-6911-50cc-a7fa-489d0b7dfea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d20f68-6911-50cc-a7fa-489d0b7dfea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447733} :answer-field/id #uuid "b79c8b14-10e4-5053-854b-9d86f75639d2" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e888d78-0912-515d-b8bd-22e159c76d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447734} {:answer/id #uuid "2cfacc3c-03da-54a1-be77-08eaf080eea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e888d78-0912-515d-b8bd-22e159c76d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447734} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae64784-a378-57b4-8dcc-e0f13a53e107" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448907}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81d16fc8-2819-579f-80e6-748f22f14098" :question/math-academy-id "q-105319" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 20 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-15{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -15 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -7 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 12 & -7 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+4(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{1}+4(\\mathbf{0})-4(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$, we get that the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” and “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” are true, while statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bd56f36-065b-5f6f-ada7-59d0d4edc3a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467232} {:answer/id #uuid "c501bb1b-5855-5fe5-aa04-343c279dda15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bd56f36-065b-5f6f-ada7-59d0d4edc3a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592