ation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -4 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” and “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” are false, while statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dfbe41c-73e7-5f56-8ce0-fab54ad50616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467286} {:answer/id #uuid "f341d81e-bf26-5210-b2f0-54763ec31dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f341d81e-bf26-5210-b2f0-54763ec31dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467287} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf382855-5600-5598-8164-5bd2d028dbce" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ 