/id #edb/ref 17592186668620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5708e06-a3e5-5159-99d8-b2272c60e24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668619} :answer-field/id #uuid "65f7c0d9-3efa-5564-8558-114d17a00978" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668887}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c6e61ad-5f9a-5a1b-a420-c0ce7a3cc35c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34700" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” is false, while statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions” and “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae02702d-cbaa-5d1a-aa13-b56e62ddc9bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467292} {:answer/id #uuid "8beff570-6962-575d-83e8-fba6dd1988f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8beff570-6962-575d-83e8-fba6dd1988f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467293} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa0b3013-1ffe-5f8b-9931-4aa005775eb9" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf5efc0-d0b0-