2186668621} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb48b3d4-fc15-569b-a755-b2995ddab156" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668888}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b1abddd4-93e9-501d-bf47-b8161bdb88cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-34714" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$, we get that the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” and “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent” are true, while statement “The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3917c546-1a71-5b69-95fa-031bd8a95f70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468148} {:answer/id #uuid "685efbb1-a98a-5e24-81fb-c69c96152f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685efbb1-a98a-5e24-81fb-c69c96152f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468149} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4d8e60-f36f-5898-86ce-56958409039b" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "799189fe-d9b2-5